1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,419
Ride three blocks east
and two blocks north.

2
00:00:03,419 --> 00:00:06,286
Then one block east and four blocks north.

3
00:00:06,286 --> 00:00:07,695
Where are you now?

4
00:00:08,095 --> 00:00:09,588
Four east, six north.

5
00:00:09,588 --> 00:00:13,421
You added the east parts together,
and the north parts together.

6
00:00:13,871 --> 00:00:18,827
Aarav rode exactly like this to college
this morning, one turn after another.

7
00:00:19,177 --> 00:00:22,192
Adding complex numbers works the same way.

8
00:00:22,192 --> 00:00:24,260
Real parts with real parts.

9
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:26,872
Imaginary parts with imaginary parts.

10
00:00:27,372 --> 00:00:31,021
Today we add, subtract,
multiply and divide them.

11
00:00:31,671 --> 00:00:33,102
First, addition.

12
00:00:33,102 --> 00:00:37,844
Take z one equals a plus i b,
and z two equals c plus i d.

13
00:00:38,194 --> 00:00:39,094
Step one.

14
00:00:38,955 --> 00:00:40,291
Add the real parts.

15
00:00:40,291 --> 00:00:41,191
a plus c.

16
00:00:41,857 --> 00:00:42,757
Step two.

17
00:00:42,734 --> 00:00:44,542
Add the imaginary parts.

18
00:00:44,542 --> 00:00:45,484
b plus d.

19
00:00:46,234 --> 00:00:47,157
Step three.

20
00:00:47,157 --> 00:00:48,493
Put them together.

21
00:00:48,493 --> 00:00:52,359
z one plus z two is a plus
c, plus i times b plus d.

22
00:00:53,109 --> 00:00:55,201
Now watch it on the address board.

23
00:00:55,551 --> 00:00:59,110
z one is an arrow from the
start to three plus two i.

24
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:01,388
z two is one plus four i.

25
00:01:01,388 --> 00:01:04,616
Slide it so it starts
where the first arrow ends.

26
00:01:05,016 --> 00:01:07,482
Its tip lands on four plus six i.

27
00:01:07,482 --> 00:01:09,472
That is z one plus z two.

28
00:01:09,872 --> 00:01:12,612
Change z two, and the sum moves with it.

29
00:01:12,612 --> 00:01:13,977
Always tip to tail.

30
00:01:14,627 --> 00:01:16,892
Subtraction is adding the opposite.

31
00:01:16,892 --> 00:01:21,007
To find z one minus z two, flip
the second arrow, then add.

32
00:01:21,657 --> 00:01:22,835
Side by side.

33
00:01:22,835 --> 00:01:25,015
Adding keeps the parts apart.

34
00:01:25,015 --> 00:01:28,023
Real with real, imaginary with imaginary.

35
00:01:28,423 --> 00:01:30,113
Multiplying mixes them.

36
00:01:30,113 --> 00:01:34,902
Every term meets every other term,
and i times i becomes minus one.

37
00:01:35,502 --> 00:01:36,402
Quick one.

38
00:01:36,385 --> 00:01:39,635
What is five plus two
i, minus three minus i?

39
00:01:39,635 --> 00:01:40,884
Pause and think.

40
00:01:44,084 --> 00:01:45,543
Two plus three i!

41
00:01:45,543 --> 00:01:47,449
Five minus three is two.

42
00:01:47,449 --> 00:01:49,933
Two i minus minus i is three i.

43
00:01:50,583 --> 00:01:55,380
Now multiply, with the NCERT example:
three plus five i, times two plus

44
00:01:55,380 --> 00:01:56,280
six i.

45
00:01:56,417 --> 00:01:57,320
Step one.

46
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:59,862
Multiply every term by every term.

47
00:01:59,862 --> 00:02:01,733
Three times two is six.

48
00:02:01,733 --> 00:02:04,232
Three times six i is eighteen i.

49
00:02:04,982 --> 00:02:05,950
Step two.

50
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:08,275
Five i times two is ten i.

51
00:02:08,275 --> 00:02:11,510
Five i times six i is thirty i squared.

52
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:13,160
Step three.

53
00:02:13,146 --> 00:02:17,064
i squared is minus one, so
thirty i squared is minus thirty.

54
00:02:17,814 --> 00:02:18,714
Step four.

55
00:02:18,709 --> 00:02:19,609
Collect.

56
00:02:19,439 --> 00:02:22,081
Six minus thirty is minus twenty four.

57
00:02:22,081 --> 00:02:24,950
Eighteen i plus ten i is twenty eight i.

58
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:29,123
So the product is minus twenty
four plus twenty eight i.

59
00:02:29,773 --> 00:02:30,940
Remember this.

60
00:02:30,940 --> 00:02:32,402
Add part by part.

61
00:02:32,402 --> 00:02:37,399
Multiply every term by every term,
and turn i squared into minus one.

62
00:02:38,099 --> 00:02:39,632
One special product.

63
00:02:39,632 --> 00:02:42,011
Multiply three plus two i by i.

64
00:02:42,011 --> 00:02:46,996
You get three i plus two i squared,
which is minus two plus three i.

65
00:02:47,396 --> 00:02:50,502
On the board, the arrow
turns a quarter turn.

66
00:02:50,502 --> 00:02:52,124
Multiplying by i turns.

67
00:02:52,124 --> 00:02:53,489
It never stretches.

68
00:02:54,139 --> 00:02:55,039
Your turn.

69
00:02:55,024 --> 00:02:56,905
One plus i, all squared.

70
00:02:56,905 --> 00:02:59,387
Is it two i, or two plus two i?

71
00:02:59,387 --> 00:03:00,638
Pause and think.

72
00:03:03,838 --> 00:03:04,738
Two i!

73
00:03:04,525 --> 00:03:06,752
One plus two i plus i squared.

74
00:03:06,752 --> 00:03:09,133
The one and the i squared cancel.

75
00:03:09,783 --> 00:03:11,208
Last, division.

76
00:03:11,208 --> 00:03:14,817
Dividing by z means
multiplying by one over z.

77
00:03:15,217 --> 00:03:19,853
NCERT gives one over z, for z
equals a plus i b, not zero.

78
00:03:19,853 --> 00:03:24,145
It is a minus i b, divided
by a squared plus b squared.

79
00:03:24,745 --> 00:03:26,860
Check it with two minus three i.

80
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:29,935
One over it is two plus
three i, over thirteen.

81
00:03:29,935 --> 00:03:33,951
Multiply them, and you get thirteen
over thirteen, which is one.

82
00:03:34,601 --> 00:03:36,336
Now, one worked example.

83
00:03:36,686 --> 00:03:42,120
Simplify one plus two i, times three
minus i, then add two minus five i.

84
00:03:42,620 --> 00:03:43,528
Step one.

85
00:03:43,528 --> 00:03:45,112
Multiply every term.

86
00:03:45,112 --> 00:03:49,044
Three, minus i, plus six
i, minus two i squared.

87
00:03:49,794 --> 00:03:50,694
Step two.

88
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:53,058
Minus two i squared is plus two.

89
00:03:53,058 --> 00:03:55,677
So the product is five plus five i.

90
00:03:56,427 --> 00:03:57,434
Step three.

91
00:03:57,434 --> 00:03:59,184
Add two minus five i.

92
00:03:59,184 --> 00:04:01,044
Five plus two is seven.

93
00:04:01,044 --> 00:04:03,309
Five i minus five i is zero.

94
00:04:04,059 --> 00:04:05,544
The answer is seven.

95
00:04:05,544 --> 00:04:09,481
The imaginary parts cancelled,
so the result is purely real.

96
00:04:10,131 --> 00:04:11,596
Now, the exam trap.

97
00:04:11,946 --> 00:04:16,632
Many students multiply two plus three
i by four plus five i, and write

98
00:04:16,632 --> 00:04:18,239
eight plus fifteen i.

99
00:04:18,639 --> 00:04:20,701
But that skips the middle terms.

100
00:04:20,701 --> 00:04:25,645
The full product is eight, plus ten i,
plus twelve i, plus fifteen i squared.

101
00:04:25,645 --> 00:04:28,098
That is minus seven plus twenty two i.

102
00:04:28,748 --> 00:04:30,316
Where is this asked?

103
00:04:30,316 --> 00:04:35,250
In JEE Main, for example in September
twenty twenty, one plus i over one

104
00:04:35,250 --> 00:04:37,418
minus i had to be simplified.

105
00:04:37,418 --> 00:04:40,553
And in PUC boards, from
this NCERT section.

106
00:04:41,153 --> 00:04:42,418
Exam level now.

107
00:04:42,418 --> 00:04:46,802
Find one plus i to the four,
plus one minus i to the four.

108
00:04:46,802 --> 00:04:48,121
Pause and solve.

109
00:04:53,521 --> 00:04:54,926
The answer is C.

110
00:04:54,926 --> 00:04:55,982
Minus eight.

111
00:04:56,482 --> 00:05:00,525
One plus i, squared, is one
plus two i plus i squared.

112
00:05:00,525 --> 00:05:01,768
That is two i.

113
00:05:02,268 --> 00:05:05,124
One minus i, squared, is minus two i.

114
00:05:05,624 --> 00:05:06,704
Square again.

115
00:05:06,704 --> 00:05:11,842
Two i squared is minus four, and minus
two i squared is also minus four.

116
00:05:11,842 --> 00:05:13,748
The total is minus eight.

117
00:05:14,348 --> 00:05:15,808
Here is your recap.

118
00:05:15,808 --> 00:05:17,309
Screenshot this card.

119
00:05:20,509 --> 00:05:23,507
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

120
00:05:23,907 --> 00:05:24,807
One.

121
00:05:24,447 --> 00:05:27,731
What is four minus i,
plus two plus five i?

122
00:05:28,631 --> 00:05:29,531
Two.

123
00:05:29,174 --> 00:05:31,483
What is i times, one plus i?

124
00:05:32,383 --> 00:05:33,283
Three.

125
00:05:33,024 --> 00:05:37,959
Why is two plus three i, times four
plus five i, not eight plus fifteen

126
00:05:37,959 --> 00:05:38,859
i?

127
00:05:39,490 --> 00:05:42,474
Next time: a mirror image across the road.

128
00:05:42,474 --> 00:05:46,140
We meet equality and the
conjugate of a complex number.
